  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - In the absence of an accurate Site Location Plan clearly indicating the application site, the schemes fails to comply with the requirements set out in Article 7(c)(i) of the Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) (England) Order 2015.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed single storey rear extension by reason of its siting, design, size, scale and mass would result in an unsympathetic, visually intrusive and incongruous form of development that fails to harmonise with the pattern of development of the locality, the character and appearance of the host property and the row of terrace it belongs to. The proposal would fail to accord with the principles of NPPF 2024 Chapters 4 and 12, London Plan 2021 policies D3 and D4, Merton Local Plan Policies D12.1, D12.3 and D12.4.",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed single storey rear extension, by reason of its combined siting, height and depth would result in a visually intrusive, overbearing and dominant form of development that would create a sense of enclosure to the detriment of the amenity of nearby occupants, in particular, no. 41 and 45 Maycross Avenue, morden. The proposals would be contrary NPPF 2024 Chapters 4 and 12, London Plan 2021 policies D3 and D4, Merton Local Plan Policies D12.1, D12.3 and D12.4.",
    "Reason : 4 - In the absence of a Flood Risk Assessment incorporating drainage strategy, it has not been demonstrated the scheme would safeguard the risk of flooding in the locality.  The proposal is contrary to, in particular, NPPF 2024 Chapter 14, London Plan 2021 policy SI 13, Merton Local Plan 2024 policies F15.7 Flood Risk Management and Sustainable Drainage, F15.8 Managing Local Flooding and F15.9 Sustainable Drainage Systems (SUDS).",
    "Reason : 5 - INFORMATIVE\r\nThe Site Location Plan is a validation requirement. The current Site Location Plan submitted is for a different address no. 41 Maycross Avenue, Morden which is not this site location. Any future resubmission would require an accurate Site Location Plan reflecting the correct Site Address.\r\n"
  ],
